---
/**
 * /privacy — Nigeria Data Protection Act / NDPR-aware privacy policy.
 *
 * ⚠️ IMPORTANT — READ BEFORE PUBLISHING
 * This policy is written to accurately describe what the site ACTUALLY does as
 * of 5 Oct 2026, based on a full review of the codebase. It is a good-faith,
 * technically accurate draft, NOT legal advice. Have it reviewed before you rely
 * on it, and UPDATE IT whenever you add analytics, ads, or a new integration.
 *
 * Two sections will become inaccurate the moment you install anything:
 *   • "Analytics" — currently none are installed
 *   • "Cookies"   — currently the site sets no first-party cookies
 * Both are flagged inline below.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, BUSINESS } from '../config/site';

const pageUrl = `${SITE.url}/privacy/`;
const lastUpdated = '5 October 2026';

const schema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebPage',
  '@id': `${pageUrl}#webpage`,
  url: pageUrl,
  name: 'Privacy Policy',
  dateModified: '2026-10-05',
  inLanguage: 'en-NG',
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How IbadanSolarHub collects, uses and protects your personal data, in line with the Nigeria Data Protection Act."
  schema={schema}
>
  <section class="bg-slate-900 text-white py-12 border-b border-slate-800">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black tracking-tight">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-400">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-14 space-y-8 text-sm text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">The Short Version</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        We collect only what you type into our quote form, we use it to connect you with a solar
        installer, and we do not sell your data to anyone. There is no tracking pixel on this
        site and no account to create.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">Who We Are</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        {BUSINESS.legalName} operates {SITE.name}. For any privacy question, or to exercise any
        right described below, contact us at
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="font-semibold text-solar-700 underline underline-offset-2">{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">What We Collect</h2>

      <h3 class="mt-4 font-bold text-slate-900">Information you give us</h3>
      <p class="mt-2">
        When you submit the quote request form we collect: your name, your phone/WhatsApp number,
        your city or neighbourhood, your property type, the system size you are interested in,
        and any appliances or notes you type in. That is the whole list — there are no hidden
        fields.
      </p>

      <h3 class="mt-4 font-bold text-slate-900">Information collected automatically</h3>
      <p class="mt-2">
        Our host (Cloudflare) processes standard technical request data — IP address, browser
        type, and pages requested — to serve the site and protect it from abuse and denial-of-service
        attacks. This is ordinary web server logging.
      </p>

      {/*
        ⚠️ UPDATE THIS SECTION WHEN YOU INSTALL ANALYTICS.
        As of the date above there is genuinely no analytics on the site.
      */}
      <div class="mt-4 rounded-xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-4">
        <p class="font-bold text-amber-900">Analytics: none currently installed</p>
        <p class="mt-1 text-amber-900">
          As of the date of this policy, this site does not run Google Analytics, Meta Pixel,
          or any other visitor-tracking service. If that changes, this section must be updated
          before the tracking goes live, and consent handling added where required.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">How Your Information Is Used</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="font-black text-solar-500" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span>To match you with a solar installer in your area and pass your requirements to them so they can prepare a quote.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="font-black text-solar-500" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span>To contact you about your enquiry.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="font-black text-solar-500" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span>To keep a record of enquiries so we can follow up if an installer does not respond.</span></li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-3">
        We do not sell, rent or trade your personal information. We do not send marketing
        messages to numbers collected through the quote form.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">Where Your Data Goes</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        This matters more than most privacy policies admit, so here is exactly where a quote
        form submission travels:
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="font-black text-solar-500" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span><strong class="text-slate-900">WhatsApp (Meta):</strong> the form opens WhatsApp with your details pre-filled. If you press send, that message is delivered through WhatsApp and is subject to Meta's own privacy terms.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="font-black text-solar-500" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span><strong class="text-slate-900">Our own lead record:</strong> a copy of your submission may be stored on Cloudflare infrastructure so we have a record of your enquiry.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="font-black text-solar-500" aria-hidden="true">→</span><span><strong class="text-slate-900">Your matched installer:</strong> we share your requirements with the installer who will quote you. They use it only to prepare and follow up that quote.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">Third-Party Links</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        We link out to retailers (Jumia, Konga), financing partners (Earthbond), and our digital
        products store (Selar). Some of these are affiliate links. Once you leave our site, the
        destination's own privacy policy and cookie policy apply — we have no control over what
        they collect. We recommend reading theirs before purchasing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">External Services We Load</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Our pages load fonts from Google Fonts. This means your browser makes a request directly
        to Google servers, which discloses your IP address to Google. We are working on
        self-hosting these fonts to remove that third-party request entirely.
      </p>
    </section>

    {/*
      ⚠️ UPDATE THIS SECTION WHEN YOU ADD COOKIES OR ANALYTICS.
    */}
    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">Cookies</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        This site does not set first-party cookies for advertising or tracking, and we do not
        run a cookie banner because we are not currently doing anything that requires consent.
        Our host may set a strictly-necessary security cookie to distinguish human visitors from
        bots. If we add analytics or advertising later, we will add a consent mechanism and
        update this policy first.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">How Long We Keep Your Data</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Quote enquiries are kept for as long as needed to handle your request and any follow-up,
        and then archived or deleted. You can ask us to delete your enquiry at any time.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">Your Rights</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Under the Nigeria Data Protection Act you have the right to access the personal data we
        hold about you, to have it corrected if inaccurate, to have it deleted, to object to or
        restrict processing, and to request a copy in a portable format. To exercise any of
        these, email
        <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="font-semibold text-solar-700 underline underline-offset-2">{SITE.email}</a>
        and we will respond within 30 days.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">Security</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        The site is served over HTTPS with HTTP Strict Transport Security enabled. Form
        submissions are transmitted over encrypted connections. No system is perfectly secure,
        but we collect as little as possible specifically so that a breach would expose as
        little as possible.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">Children</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        This site is intended for adults arranging solar installations. We do not knowingly
        collect data from anyone under 18.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-slate-900">Changes to This Policy</h2>
      <p class="mt-3">
        If we change how we handle your data we will update this page and revise the date at the
        top. Material changes affecting data we already hold will be communicated to affected
        individuals directly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-6">
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 leading-relaxed">
        <strong class="text-slate-700">Note for the site owner:</strong> this policy accurately
        reflects the codebase as reviewed. It is not a substitute for legal advice. Have it
        reviewed by a Nigerian lawyer, and re-check the Analytics, Cookies and Third-Party
        sections whenever you add a new integration.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
